 ProcessTool_WithMenubar;globalParms;list;parms;result;n
⍝ Presents a list of any length and allows processing selected rows by selecting a command form the menu bar.
 globalParms←##.APLGUI.APLGuiGlobalParms.CreateDefaults
 globalParms.regKey←'MyApp'
 globalParms.caption←'My App'
 globalParms.icon←#.⎕NEW'Icon'(⊂'File'(GetFile'Sample.ico'))
 list←∪300⍴#.⎕NL-3
 list←list[⍋⊃list]
 parms←##.APLGUI.ProcessTool.CreateParms
 parms.caption←'Process selected items'
 parms.colTitles←,⊂'Numbers'
 parms.style←##.APLGUI.Enums.SelectionStyles.multi
 parms.info←'Select as many items as you like and then select "Process my items" from the "Special" menu'
 parms.useWindowsRegistry←1
 parms.processBtnCaption←''
 parms.menuCaption←'Special'
 parms.menuItemCaptions←'Process my items' 'aaa' '1111'
 parms.dblClick←0
 parms.default←(⍳≢list)∊3?≢list
 n←globalParms parms ##.APLGUI.ProcessTool.Create list'##.##.##.APLGUI.APLGUI_Demo∆OnTestHandler_ProcessTool'

 result←##.APLGUI.ProcessTool.ModalWait n
 ⎕←(⍕result),' item(s) were processed'
